-### WGAR@1 — smoke test (interactive, ~5 min on L40S)
+# Whitebox Attack Code
+
+The publishable experiment is implemented in `whitebox_attack/v3/`.
+
+Earlier top-level scripts (pre-v3 wrong-gap-assessment experiments, old
+sbatch files, and old logs) have been moved to
+`whitebox_attack/archive/pre_v3_root_20260910/` (2026-09-10 cleanup). They
+are not part of the final v3 production matrix unless a paper appendix
+explicitly cites them. Two root-level files were kept in place because they
+are live dependencies of the active v3 runtime, not legacy artifacts:
+`metrics.py` (imported by `v3/production_runner.py`) and `cue_definitions.py`
+(imported by `v3/cues.py`).
+
+The canonical analysis for completed model families is
+`whitebox_attack/v3/analysis/` (see its own `README.md`); its output lives
+in `whitebox_paper_results/e2e_full_system_v3/production/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260910/`.
+Older one-off evaluation directories under `.../evaluation/` were moved to
+`.../evaluation/_archive_superseded_20260910/` in the same cleanup.
+
+## Final v3 Modules
+
+- `v3/production_models.py`: final model allowlist and model-specific parser map.
+- `v3/production_manifest.py`: frozen 450-example manifests for each dataset.
+- `v3/cues.py`: final condition registry and suffix hashes.
+- `v3/benchmark_search.py`: deterministic benchmark-local retrieval adapter.
+- `v3/runner.py`: ODR invocation and trace capture.
+- `v3/runtime_gate.py`: embedded pre-shard runtime validation.
+- `v3/production_runner.py`: SLURM array shard runner.
+- `v3/generate_v3_qwen_cluster_arrays.py`: final matrix, sbatch, validation, and
+  duplicate-safe submission generator.
+- `v3/final_production_evaluation.py`: aggregate offline evaluator for final
+  PCR, direct-answer bypass, inclusive premature termination, tool choice, and
+  answer accuracy.
+
+## Safety During Active Production Jobs
+
+Queued SLURM jobs import the v3 runtime modules and `open_deep_research` package
+from the current working tree. Do not edit those runtime files while final jobs
+are queued or running unless the jobs are cancelled and resubmitted from the
+updated code.
+
+Documentation-only edits and quarantine moves for ignored validation artifacts
+are safe.
